#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2270 expect=noViolation domain=DD
#note "PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK18 (3) (owner 2026-10-11): DS without USUBJID does NOT reach the QK16 ERROR for FDA-SE2270 - the Check's leading `USUBJID in $ds_usubjid` reads distinct(USUBJID, domain=\"DS\"), which holds no subject when DS lacks the column, so the conjunct is false on every record and the grouped DS extreme (group=[USUBJID]) is never read. Pinned as the measured answer: silent, no ERROR. Why it is data-dependent here (owner QK19, 2026-10-11): FDA-SE2270 has a rule-level Grouping, whose path has no absent-column fold reading the bindings up front, so the lazy grouped binding is read only behind the and short-circuit (E2) - the same Check without the Grouping ERRORs on this shape (measured on FDA-SE2270). A gate declaring DS.USUBJID would turn it into a SKIP."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DD label="Death Diagnosis"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DDSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DDTESTCD type=Char label="Death Diagnosis Short Name"
col DDORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col DDDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Collection"
col DDDY     type=Num  label="Study Day of Collection"
---
S1 | DD | 001 | 1 | DTHCAUS | HEPATIC NECROSIS | 2020-01-18 | 18
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
col DSSTDY  type=Num  label="Study Day of Start of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 1 | FOUND DEAD | DEAD | 2020-01-20 | 20

